<h1 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 1 – Lesson # 1</h1>
<p style="text-align: center; font-style: italic;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Following Instructions at School</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> First, I Cut the Paper.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Follow clear instructions in learning activities. Interactive: Execute multi-step directions in learning activities.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can follow clear instructions in learning activities to complete a task (e.g., "First, cut the paper, then glue it on the flowchart."). Can follow and respond to multi-step directions in-class activities (e.g., "You need to fold the paper before you cut it."). Can respond appropriately to oral instructions (e.g., "Let's put away our books.").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows realia (paper, scissors, glue, pencil) and asks, "What are these?" and "What can we make with them?" Students brainstorm simple craft items (e.g., "a mask," "a card"). The teacher leads a quick "Simon Says" activity focusing on classroom actions and items: "Simon says: Touch your <b>p</b>en<b>c</b>il!" "Simon says: Hold your <b>p</b>a<b>p</b>er." (Embedding /p/ and /s/ pronunciation.)</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary words: "<b>p</b>a<b>p</b>er," "<b>s</b>ci<b>ss</b>or<b>s</b>," "<b>g</b>lue," "<b>c</b>u<b>t</b>," "<b>p</b>a<b>s</b>te," "<b>f</b>old," "<b>d</b>raw." The teacher clearly articulates the /p/ sound in "paper" and "paste" and the /s/ sound in "scissors" and "mask." The teacher also models multi-step instructions using actions, like "First, I fold the paper. Next, I cut." while performing the actions. The teacher uses flashcards for each new word.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of new vocabulary and instructions.
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Showing scissors) "Is this glue or scissors?" (Expected: "Scissors!")</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Teacher folds paper) "Am I cutting or folding the paper?" (Expected: "Folding!")</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Demonstrating) "When I say 'First, cut,' what do you do first?" (Expected: "Cut!")</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Following Instructions at School")</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Audio recording of a teacher giving simple, clear, multi-step instructions for a craft project. The audio is at A1.3 level, featuring common classroom verbs and craft nouns. It includes sequencing words ("first, next, then") and plural imperatives ("Let's make a poster.").</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: To understand and follow short, simple oral instructions related to classroom activities and school projects.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions (First Listening):</b> Students listen to the audio and circle the main item being made (e.g., "Is it a mask or a card?").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Second Listening):</b> The teacher plays the audio again. Students listen and mark T/F for statements like: "First, they cut the paper. (T/F)" "They paste the drawing. (T/F)"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching (Third Listening):</b> Students are given pictures representing steps (e.g., a hand cutting, a hand gluing). They listen to the audio a third time and match the picture to the sequencing word they hear (e.g., "First" with cutting picture, "Next" with gluing picture).</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice listening for specific instructions, identifying sequencing words, and associating spoken commands with physical actions. Focus on plural imperatives ("Let's make a poster."), sequencing words ("first, next"), future tense ("I will make a mask."), and target vocabulary (paper, scissors, glue, cut, fold, paste, draw, mask, card).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: Listen and Point:</b> The teacher says single instructions (e.g., "Cut the paper," "Paste the glue," "Draw a mask," "Fold it small"). Students listen and point to the correct flashcard or item on their desks. The teacher repeats, emphasizing /p/ and /s/ sounds. (Focus on individual word recognition and simple commands).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: Listen and Number/Sequence:</b> Students receive a handout with 3-4 simple action pictures (e.g., a hand folding paper, a hand cutting, a hand gluing). The teacher reads a sequence of instructions, using "First, Next, Then" (e.g., "First, fold the paper. Next, cut the paper. Then, paste the paper."). Students listen and number the pictures in the correct order. The teacher checks answers orally: "What is first?" "What is next?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction / Peer Check: Listen and Do:</b> In pairs, one student (A) gives a simple, one-step instruction using target vocabulary (e.g., "Cut the paper," "Draw a big mask," "Fold it"). The other student (B) listens and performs the action with imaginary or real supplies. They then switch roles. The teacher circulates, observing listening comprehension and pronunciation. The teacher prompts students to use future intentions: "What will you make?" "I will make a mask!" and clarification: "What do I need to do next?"</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Following Instructions at School")</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Guided Craft Activity (Individual/Pair Work).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will follow a multi-step audio instruction to create a simple paper craft, like a "small colorful card" or a "paper mask." The teacher provides each student with a piece of paper, safety scissors (or pre-cut shapes), and glue. The instructions are pre-recorded and played step-by-step, allowing pauses for students to complete each action.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher plays an audio recording with instructions (e.g., "Hello, class! Today, we will make a small card. First, fold your paper in half. Next, draw a big heart on the front. Then, cut the heart. Finally, paste a small decoration inside. You will make a beautiful card!").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students listen to each instruction and perform the action. The teacher pauses the audio after each step to allow students time to complete it.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher monitors, providing minimal help and encouraging students to ask for clarification if needed ("What do I need to do next?").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">When finished, students can share their creations. The teacher asks, "What did you make?" "I made a card!" "I will make another mask!"</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students display their completed paper crafts. The teacher observes students' ability to follow the multi-step audio instructions during the production phase.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Observation Checklist):</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student correctly followed "first" instruction.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student correctly followed "next" instruction.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student correctly followed subsequent instructions.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student used appropriate materials (paper, scissors, glue).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student attempted to ask for clarification if confused.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket by circling a smiley face and answering:
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Was it easy to follow the instructions? (Yes / A little / No)</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was the first thing you did? (e.g., "I folded the paper.")</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b> The teacher asks the class:
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new words did you learn today?"</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was fun about following instructions?"</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this listening lesson? (e.g., TPR, visual aids, clear audio instructions).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to further support students' listening comprehension? (e.g., shorter instructions, more pauses, clearer pronunciation of specific sounds).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students effectively use sequencing words and respond to imperatives?</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2, students will read short, illustrated texts with instructions that include the same vocabulary (paper, scissors, glue, cut, fold, paste) and sequencing words (first, next, then) to understand how written instructions are structured, building on their listening comprehension from this lesson.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>